# Requirements

## Hypotheses

### H1: Each of c2, c3, c4 held at 1 alone moves the body

WHEN exactly one of the constant levels a2, a3, a4 is 1 and all other levels are 0 for the whole trial, THE system SHALL change x by at least 0.05 m in magnitude for at least one of them.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 0.0
a1 = 0.0
a2 = 0.0
a3 = 1.0
a4 = 0.0
```

Result: rejected (see E1 verdict). c2, c3, c4 held constant each give |x| under 0.04 m.

### H2: A phase-shifted sine on all channels drives the body forward

WHEN all five channels carry a sine of amplitude 1 at 2 Hz with phase step 2*pi/5 between neighbouring channels, THE system SHALL end with x above 0.05 m.

```prediction
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.05, 3.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a0 = 1.0
a1 = 1.0
a2 = 1.0
a3 = 1.0
a4 = 1.0
f = 2.0
ph = 1.2566
```

Result: rejected. x was -0.33, -0.30, -0.10 m and the body spun.

### H3: c1 at -1 drives the body forward and c0 adjusts heading

WHEN c1 is held at -1 and the other channels are 0 for the whole trial, THE system SHALL move the body forward by 0.1 to 0.4 m and turn it clockwise by 20 to 60 degrees.

